  "rationale": "Clifford Jordan's third Blue Note album as a leader and a classic of the late-1950s hard bop quintet format. Consensus pick: AllMusic 4★ (Lee Bloom review calls it 'a wonderfully relaxed recording'), Penguin Guide to Jazz Recordings 3★. The session assembles an elite hard bop frontline (Jordan, Art Farmer) with the crack rhythm section of Sonny Clark, George Tucker, and Louis Hayes. Jordan's originals ('Laconia', 'Soul-Lo Blues', 'Cliff Craft') sit alongside bop standards by Parker, Gillespie, and Ellington. Part of Blue Note's celebrated 1500-series from one of the label's most fertile periods.",
